@* Marga, saying something (MARGA-1).

   She is a CHARACTER, not an assistant: every line she says is a localized resource string with
   real data in its placeholders. There is no model behind her and nothing here generates text —
   callers pass the finished sentence in.

   One component so no screen re-spells how she sits beside a line. Give it a size; the rest follows.
*@

<div class="marga @(Compact ? "marga-compact" : null)" data-testid="marga">
    @* Decorative: the sentence beside her carries the whole meaning, and a screen reader reading
       "photo of a bartender" before it would only get in the way. *@
    <img src="_content/JiggerJot.Shared.Ui/brand/marga_avatar_160.png" alt="" aria-hidden="true"
         class="marga-face" width="@Size" height="@Size" />
    <div class="marga-line">
        @ChildContent
        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Aside))
        {
            <span class="marga-aside">@Aside</span>
        }
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The sentence she says — already localized, already filled in.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Rendered small and quiet under the line: who said it, or when.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Aside { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Her size in pixels. 24 in a list row, 40 on a card.</summary>
    [Parameter] public int Size { get; set; } = 40;

    /// <summary>Tighter spacing and smaller text, for use inside a row rather than as a card.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Compact { get; set; }
}
